+## [Unreleased]
+
+### pi
+
+The installer knows the pi coding agent now, as `python3 install.py pi`. pi reads
+the shared `.agents/skills/` folder, so the fewest-directory rule covers it
+there; `--exact` writes to pi's own `~/.pi/agent/skills/` or a project's
+`.pi/skills/` instead. SKILL.md names pi in its compatibility line and its
+Workflow section, and adds pi's own invocation, `/skill:human-voice`. pi has no
+built-in MCP client, so the skill takes its script branch there instead of
+waiting on the `lint_prose` and `check_invariants` tools.
+
+### The invariant diff from the command line
+
+`scripts/check_invariants.py` gives shell-based agents the fact check that only
+the MCP tool and `humanize.py`'s loop could run before. It compares a rewrite
+against its original and lists the numbers, links, inline code, fenced code and
+citations that went missing, plus the numbers, links and citations that appeared
+from nowhere. It exits 1 while either list is non-empty, so it works as a gate.
+`--context` marks author material as sourced, which the MCP tool never exposed,
+and `--json` and `--quiet` cover CI and agent use. Step 9 of SKILL.md points at
+it, and the Workflow's tool-fallback section now maps every MCP tool to its
+script.
+
